# Screenshot originals. `npm run shots` converts these to .webp, which is what
# the site actually serves — committing multi-megabyte PNGs alongside would
# bloat the repo permanently, since git history keeps them even after deletion.
# Keep the originals locally so the optimizer can be re-run.
public/shots/*.png
public/shots/*.jpg
public/shots/*.jpeg
.env*

# Claude Code local settings. Accumulates whatever tool permissions you grant
# over time and is named .local because it is per-machine — it should never be
# world-readable in a public repo.
.claude/settings.local.json

# iCloud sync duplicates. This repo lives under a synced Desktop folder, and a
# sync conflict leaves a "name 2.ext" copy beside the real file. They never
# reach a commit from here, but they do break builds: two copies of
# .next/types/cache-life.d.ts both declare module 'next/cache', and the build
# fails with "Duplicate identifier". Ignoring them keeps `git add -A` clean if
# one ever lands outside a build directory.
#
# Caveat: this also ignores a genuine file named "Chapter 2.md". Nothing here
# is named that way; `git add -f` if that ever changes.
* [0-9].*
